# Honor README.md

`README.md` at the repository root is the **binding source of truth** for this Godot cowboy platformer: gameplay rules, campaign/level design, canyon and mover conventions, UI/art style, i18n (German default), and audio.

## Before changing those areas

1. **Read or consult `README.md`** (especially Core gameplay, World / level design rules, UI / art style, Audio, Agent / contributor rules, and rules 11–15).
2. **Do not violate** documented rules. Examples of forbidden regressions:
   - Calling canyons “pits” in user-facing text
   - English as the default language
   - Featureless black canyon interiors, or canyon rims covering desert floor banks
   - Black or sky gaps under dune slope crusts (sparse earth tiling)
   - Impossible canyon gaps (no hop/mover chain within normal jump reach)
   - Ferry-raft / ferry-step look on Level 4 movers (use clouds + planks)
   - Uncapped runaway wind
   - Generic flat UI that breaks the handmade western style
   - Re-deriving cowgirl on-foot sprites from cowboy frames
   - Workshop placement ghosts at grid-cell size instead of final stamp size
   - Removing workshop right-click erase or chevron grid collapse
   - Treasure chests smaller than the documented ~109% player-height scale
   - Player idle flicker from alternating mismatched idle pose frames
3. Prefer the README checklist over older chat memory or outdated cycle notes.

## When a documented rule must change

If implementing something that **requires** changing a rule already written in `README.md`, **update `README.md` in the same change** so docs and code stay aligned. Do not silently diverge.
